window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Nothing has gone to plan.</p> <p>Not a single thing.</p> <p>I entered Poseidon’s palace with one intention—steal a legendary ship and sail it to the darkest, most dangerous depths of the ocean, to try to save my sister.</p> <p>And now I am fighting for my life in a series of deadly trials designed for water gods and sea monsters, not broken, powerless nymphs.</p> <p>I was prepared for risk. I was prepared for danger.</p> <p>I was not prepared for Poseidon, or the soul-deep connection I have with him. His tenuous control teeters closer to the edge the more time I spend with him, and gods help me, I’m starting to hope that he falls—and takes me with him. </p> <p><b><i>Surrender of the Brutal King</i></b><b> is the second book in the Poseidon Trials trilogy. Expect magic, mythology, and a searing slow-burn enemies-to-lovers romance that will leave you desperate for more.</b></p>"; 
